{
  "id": "spr_voltail",
  "kind": "object",
  "type": "sprite",
  "name": "Voltail sprite",
  "notes": "Voltail, a yellow ferret with a head the same size as Emberpup's (14 px wide from the front and back, 6 rows tall, with small round ears on top at its corners) and a round brown patch around each eye that stays inside the head's outline, yellow fur between the patches and a cream muzzle with a small dark nose below them, as on its menu portrait (from the side and the left the head is Emberpup's side-head size too: both round ears on top, the patch circling the eye, the cream muzzle in front and the cream throat under it), legs 2 px wide in every view (a yellow leg over a brown paw, then a 2 px sole; from the front and back two legs, from the side a front and a back leg), and a lightning-bolt tail, drawn in the style of the monsters that walk around in GBA monster games: dark closed outline, 3 shades lit from the top-left, eyes with a glint. Seen from 8 directions: the front (down), the back (up), the side (right), the three-quarter views (down-right: the face turned right; up-right: the back turned right) and their left versions. The left views are drawn on their own, not mirrored by the engine: the shapes and the face mirror, but the shading stays lit from the top-left like every other view. Each view has a standing frame, a breathing frame (1 px lower), a blink, the frames it steps (back or left foot up, passing pose 1 px higher, other foot up, passing pose) with, and an attack lunge (no open mouth: the face stays as it is). Every frame stays inside the 16x16 box with its outline closed, so nothing is ever cut at the edges. Too many frames to keep whole in video memory: it streams (only the frames on screen are loaded).",
